# Docker build-context hygiene.
#
# On a developer machine this monorepo is ~13G (Flutter build output, APKs and
# pnpm node_modules), so an unpruned context is impractically slow to send to
# the daemon and would leak a host `node_modules` into images.
#
# IMPORTANT: services/*/dist and packages/*/dist are deliberately NOT ignored.
# services/Dockerfile.multi copies those prebuilt artifacts into the final
# images, so ignoring `dist` would produce images with no compiled code.

.git
.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log

# Dependency and bundler output — every Dockerfile installs/compiles what it needs.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage

# TypeScript incremental state. A `tsconfig.tsbuildinfo` copied from a developer machine is
# worse than useless in a build context: packages/database sets `composite: true`, so tsc reads
# the stale file, decides the project is already built, reports success *without emitting*, and
# the next package to compile fails with TS2307 "Cannot find module '@nova/database'" against a
# dist/ that was never written. The failure looks like a broken import graph and is really a
# stale artifact, which is why this line exists rather than a note in a README.
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Flutter / Android build output (apps/mobile)
apps/mobile/build
apps/mobile/.dart_tool
apps/mobile/android/build
apps/mobile/android/.gradle
apps/mobile/android/app/build
**/*.apk
**/*.aab
**/*.apk.sha1

# Expo / React Native leftovers in apps/mobile are not built
apps/mobile/.expo
